TEXT 984 -152 Left 2 ;PURPOSE:\n* Passes a range of frequencies between fL and fH\n* Attenuates frequencies below fL and above fH\n \n* STRUCTURE:\n* High-pass stage (C2, R2)\n* Low-pass stage (R1, C1)\n \n* LOWER CUTOFF (HPF):\n* fL = 1 / (2*pi*R1*C1)\n \n* UPPER CUTOFF (LPF):\n* fH = 1 / (2*pi*R2*C2)\n \n* CENTRE FREQUENCY:\n* f0 = sqrt(fL * fH)\n \n* BW = fH - fL\n \n* Q = f0 / BW\n \n* TRANSFER FUNCTION:\n* H(s) = (s*R1*C1) / [(1 + s*R1*C1)(1 + s*R2*C2)]\n \n* EXPECTED RESPONSE:\n* Low freq -> attenuated (HPF blocks)\n* Mid freq -> passes (peak around f0)\n* High freq -> attenuated (LPF blocks)\n \n* BODE SLOPES:\n* +20 dB/dec before passband\n* -20 dB/dec after passband\n \n* NOTE (RTA CONTEXT):\n* Basic model of band-pass behaviour\n* RTA CLPS uses MFB band-pass (active, higher Q)\n* RTA CLINK uses Sallen-Key HPF + LPF
TEXT 128 136 Left 2 ;LPF
TEXT 344 136 Left 2 ;HPF
TEXT 104 -56 Left 2 ;1st Order Band-Pass Filter
